{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview","id":1072706,"title":"April update and preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-03T14:39:19-07:00","id":1072706,"title":"April update and preview","content":"Fresh off the presses: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/scion-2nd-edition-tabletop-rpg/posts/1849448\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/1849448</a><br /> <br /> I'm not super shocked it isn't going to make the May date, schedule slippage happens, but how about that preview? That was a pretty meaty one, I liked the plurality of satyr paths being done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T14:56:36-07:00","id":1072711,"title":"","content":"I'm also stoked to see so many satyr varieties, as the usual one leaves me cold.<br /> <br /> And I'm fine with a delay if it means a better end product; here's hoping this means the Pantheons can all be their best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T14:57:03-07:00","id":1072712,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the previews are appreciated.<br /> <br /> And heck, back during the Q&amp;A I asked Neall how the new Geasa would work. He said &quot;Why don't I work Geasa into a preview?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, he finally delivered!<br /> <br /> Edit: And as a survivor of the Ex3 Kickstarter... Well let's just say it'll take SOME time before the delay feels 'long'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:12:53-07:00","id":1072721,"title":"","content":"Disappointing about the delay. But this update softens the blow quite a bit. I love the lore section, it nicely sets the tone for Scion/mortal interactions but leaves the scope flexible enough for different story styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:25:53-07:00","id":1072726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072712#post1072712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And as a survivor of the Ex3 Kickstarter... Well let's just say it'll take SOME time before the delay feels 'long'.</div> </div> </div> </div>[stares wistfully at Wraith20]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:31:22-07:00","id":1072729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072726#post1072726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [stares wistfully at Wraith20]</div> </div> </div> </div>*Toasts you a glass of Coke* Endure, brave fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:41:33-07:00","id":1072736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072726#post1072726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [stares wistfully at Wraith20]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One day, jakki. One day. But hey, Exalted finally has a schedule of releases and both Cursed Necropolis: Rio and the Dark Eras Companion hit, perhaps the time of these projects to move is upon us. Sothis ascends and the ancient gamelines and projects stir to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:55:06-07:00","id":1072821,"title":"","content":"If a Tuatha Scion puts a geis on a mortal during combat, I'm assuming that mortal is already in a situation that qualifies as a life-or-death situation, so how would breaking the geis escalate from there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:00:05-07:00","id":1072825,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I must have been reading the wrong Huldra legends? I don't recall them having that much of a connection to hearth and home or being quiet hermits...<br /> <br /> What happened to all the stories about them marrying mortal men and their tails falling off in a Church wedding, or of a Huldra-wife who twists a red hot poker into a pretzel to show her abusive husband what's what? Or of the shepherd boy who meets one and is polite by telling her her petticoat is showing when it actually is her cow tail?<br /> <br /> Easy enough to pick and mix knacks though.<br /> <br /> If we are going by descriptive words: Shy and Reclusive are certainly correct, so kudos to Neall, but so are Beautiful (as the Scandinavian equivalent to nymphs), Frighteningly Strong, and Kind (Especially to Charcoal Burners and those who are polite)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 04-03-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:34:58-07:00","id":1072855,"title":"","content":"Yeah, delays are always disappointing, but it seems like it's a delay that will be worth it in the end. And if Neall and his team deliver on this promise that the delay is a mere weeks or months at worst, then that's just a relatively minor delay that will ultimately make the game better in the long run. When we finally get these PDFs, and they're all kinds of amazing, I'm sure none of us will spend much time dwelling on a short delay.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd these latest previews are AWESOME! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI love the Satyr types. Each one is really unique and distinct from the others, and I can imagine all kinds of fun playing as, and playing with, all three of them. Although, I must agree with prototype00: I don't remember reading any Hulder myths that remind me of this writeup. I've definitely heard the myths he described, but I never go quite the feel about them that this writeup presents.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Purviews? Always a treat. We've already seen a lot of the Fire Boons before, but hey! They're all awesome. I have yet to see a Boon from this game that conveys that disappointed feeling of &quot;When the heck am I going to use THIS?&quot; that so often plagued the 1E Purviews. I love how Heaven's Fire basically gives you unlimited fireballs for one Legend commitment for a scene. I'm already imagining the fun of flying around, getting my Green Goblin on, nuking everything around me with big booms!<br /> <br /> \u200bForge? Love it! Once again, not a useless Boon in the mix, and it's so easy to see how much fun it will be to play a crafter Scion in this game. I'm normally not the &quot;crafter guy&quot; in our games, but even I can see myself having fun with these powers.<br /> <br /> \u200bYoga? Very cool. I love that it actually encourages you toward selfless action, and the powers are useful and interesting. And I love that they mentioned the possibility of gaining a bow that shoots nukes! Dang! The Devas don't play!<br /> <br /> \u200bOne question about Yoga? The preview mentions &quot;performing austerities&quot; as a way to fulfill one's obligations. I've heard the term before, but I'm not quite clear on what it involves? What are austerities? What are some examples of the things one might do?<br /> <br /> \u200bGeas? Still awesome, two editions running! Are we going to get more Geas options for possible consequences for broken Geasa? The preview just says you lose all your Legend points. I can certainly imagine that that's what happened to Cu Chulainn in his final battle, but will there be other possible consequences?<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd finally, the World stuff? Also great. This is what makes games interesting to me: thinking about what it would be like to live in this kind of world. Trying to imagine how it would be different from our own world. THIS is the stuff that makes game books fun to read for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:50:24-07:00","id":1072861,"title":"","content":"Aren't austerities like the mortification of the flesh performed by ascetics today? Smearing your skin with the ashes of the dead, maintaining an uncomfortable position or subsisting on basically nothing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T18:57:55-07:00","id":1072865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072861#post1072861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't austerities like the mortification of the flesh performed by ascetics today? Smearing your skin with the ashes of the dead, maintaining an uncomfortable position or subsisting on basically nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, according to our good friend, Wikipedia, that's certainly one facet of it. In general, it appears to just be a series of self-discipline practices. Meditation and study are also valid austerities, it would seem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:13:20-07:00","id":1072872,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping we see that revised Netjer draft soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:16:39-07:00","id":1072875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072865#post1072865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell, according to our good friend, Wikipedia, that's certainly one facet of it. In general, it appears to just be a series of self-discipline practices. Meditation and study are also valid austerities, it would seem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. Forgot that mortification of the Mind also counts.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Hulder, I feel obliged to point to Neil Gaiman's Monarch of the Glen novella for an excellent example of a Huldra in a modern context. The competing strains of wanting to be a solitary, reclusive wilderness existence vs wanting to be a part of society are really strong there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:22:01-07:00","id":1072878,"title":"","content":"Right! And Gaiman's work has already been specifically mentioned as one of the big inspirations for 2E! That's probably where that part is coming from.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:27:43-07:00","id":1072880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072872#post1072872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping we see that revised Netjer draft soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking that's one of the Pantheons that needed the major revision...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:37:28-07:00","id":1072884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072878#post1072878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right! And Gaiman's work has already been specifically mentioned as one of the big inspirations for 2E! That's probably where that part is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if Neall based the entire Hulder write up on the Novella, then? I mean the various extant myths have much merit too (and aspects of them obviously appear in the Novella but I still don't recall the &quot;House and Home&quot; parts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:47:32-07:00","id":1072888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072884#post1072884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if Neall based the entire Hulder write up on the Novella, then? I mean the various extant myths have much merit too (and aspects of them obviously appear in the Novella but I still don't recall the &quot;House and Home&quot; parts)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCould be. I suppose it's also possible they'll work it in so that both the classical mythology aspects and the Gaiman stuff will apply. I mean, there isn't anything in this preview that makes it impossible for the classical stuff to apply, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:12:48-07:00","id":1072898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072888#post1072888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bCould be. I suppose it's also possible they'll work it in so that both the classical mythology aspects and the Gaiman stuff will apply. I mean, there isn't anything in this preview that makes it impossible for the classical stuff to apply, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough, like I said, easy enough to mix and match knacks. Though I am slightly bummed that their custom power is &quot;Make my home a fortress&quot; Rather than &quot;I am strong enough to pretzel iron pokers or straighten horseshoes with my bare hands, so don't test me, husband mine.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:22:15-07:00","id":1072902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072898#post1072898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True enough, like I said, easy enough to mix and match knacks. Though I am slightly bummed that their custom power is &quot;Make my home a fortress&quot; Rather than &quot;I am strong enough to pretzel iron pokers or straighten horseshoes with my bare hands, so don't test me, husband mine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, but since that only appeared in one myth, it's possible that great strength isn't necessarily a defining trait for Hulder. Maybe the one in that myth just had a pretty high Strength rating, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:44:41-07:00","id":1072911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072855#post1072855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYoga? Very cool. I love that it actually encourages you toward selfless action, and the powers are useful and interesting. And I love that they mentioned the possibility of gaining a bow that shoots nukes! Dang! The Devas don't play!<br /> <br /> \u200bOne question about Yoga? The preview mentions &quot;performing austerities&quot; as a way to fulfill one's obligations. I've heard the term before, but I'm not quite clear on what it involves? What are austerities? What are some examples of the things one might do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yoga is fricking AWESOME!!! And much as I know that Devotion's Reward is probably going to be everyone's pick for the Nuke-shooting bow possibilities, I LOVE Eyes of Knowledge...the ability to see through divine bullshit into the heart of why the Gods are doing something is awesome!<br /> <br /> As for the austerities, put very simply, engaging in any form of Yoga to the exclusion of all else counts as an austerity...this can mean spending time in intense contemplation of scripture or the universe for Jnana Yoga, single minded devotion or ecstatic dances and trances in honour of a God for Bhakti Yoga, absolute dedication to your duties or performing selfless service to those in need for Karma Yoga, or meditation and physical and mental self-control for Hatha/Ashtanga Yoga (a.k.a. the only Yoga as far as most of the West is concerned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). If you've ever heard stories of Hindus sitting meditating for long stretches of time without eating or the like, that's an austerity...the not-eating and other privation isn't usually the point, but rather a side effect of the single minded contemplation/devotion/action/meditation etc.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd like to point out that calling them pathways kinda gives the impression that they're mutually exclusive, when that totally isn't the case...people can and do practice different kinds of Yoga. It is in fact the norm to do that...a man could get up in the morning and practice Hatha Yoga exercises, then go in to work to do his duty as a Karma Yogi, then get back home and worship at his household altar, for Bhakti Yoga, and then curl up with a book and think about the universe for Jnana Yoga before falling asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T20:54:22-07:00","id":1072916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072911#post1072911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, I'd like to point out that calling them pathways kinda gives the impression that they're mutually exclusive, when that totally isn't the case...people can and do practice different kinds of Yoga. It is in fact the norm to do that...a man could get up in the morning and practice Hatha Yoga exercises, then go in to work to do his duty as a Karma Yogi, then get back home and worship at his household altar, for Bhakti Yoga, and then curl up with a book and think about the universe for Jnana Yoga before falling asleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would this phrasing be more accurate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The yog\u00e1s are disciplines that cultivate the liberation of the spirit and realization of the ultimate self through selfless action (k\u00e1rma y\u00f3ga), personal devotion to divinities (bhakti y\u00f3ga) and the pursuit of understanding the divine (j\u00f1ana y\u00f3ga).</span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T21:25:43-07:00","id":1072924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1072706-april-update-and-preview?p=1072916#post1072916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would this phrasing be more accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I actually like that one better...being multi-disciplinary is totally a thing, and just the word discipline in all it's forms kinda better...resonates, I guess, with the concepts of Yoga. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count